1
00:00:00,644 --> 00:00:05,223
Recruiting outreach fails in boring, expensive ways: duplicate messages,

2
00:00:05,223 --> 00:00:08,212
dead endpoints, and no record of what was sent.

3
00:00:08,486 --> 00:00:13,571
Reachout is a self-hosted recruiting CRM that runs that work across WhatsApp and email,

4
00:00:13,571 --> 00:00:15,499
with the audit trail to prove it.

5
00:00:17,263 --> 00:00:18,823
Setup is three steps.

6
00:00:18,823 --> 00:00:22,240
Python 3.10 or newer, uv sync for the backend,

7
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,063
then one uvicorn command on port 8000.

8
00:00:25,518 --> 00:00:28,057
The first start creates the SQLite database.

9
00:00:28,057 --> 00:00:32,558
The same FastAPI process serves the API and the dashboard, with no build step.

10
00:00:33,099 --> 00:00:36,088
The repository ships unit, integration and browser tests.

11
00:00:36,088 --> 00:00:37,819
This is the recorded backend run.

12
00:00:39,253 --> 00:00:44,613
This is the seeded demo database: twenty-five contacts, fifty endpoints,

13
00:00:44,613 --> 00:00:46,846
forty attempts, all synthetic.

14
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:50,628
Overview answers who still needs a message, what failed,

15
00:00:50,628 --> 00:00:52,457
and what is due for follow-up.

16
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:57,729
The campaign deck shows the active run, its target, and attempt counters for sent,

17
00:00:57,729 --> 00:00:59,043
failed and unresolved.

18
00:00:59,462 --> 00:01:01,407
Contacts are grouped by company.

19
00:01:01,407 --> 00:01:06,087
The dispatcher reaches one person per company before it returns for a second.

20
00:01:06,495 --> 00:01:10,481
Every phone number and email is a separate endpoint with its own state,

21
00:01:10,481 --> 00:01:12,783
so one dead address never hides the rest.

22
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:14,781
Open send, and the endpoint,

23
00:01:14,781 --> 00:01:19,366
sender and rendered template are all chosen before anything leaves the machine.

24
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,623
Templates keep each message body in one place,

25
00:01:22,623 --> 00:01:25,094
with variables that fill in per contact.

26
00:01:25,508 --> 00:01:30,049
Failures stay visible, with masked destinations, the failure reason,

27
00:01:30,049 --> 00:01:31,651
and the attempt history.

28
00:01:33,299 --> 00:01:36,049
A real send now, from this machine to a second account,

29
00:01:36,049 --> 00:01:37,499
so the whole path is visible.

30
00:01:37,818 --> 00:01:41,938
Camoufox opens WhatsApp Web, finds the chat, and types the rendered message.

31
00:01:42,254 --> 00:01:46,294
It leaves under the same spacing, retry and audit rules as any campaign send.

32
00:01:46,618 --> 00:01:50,938
Email takes the same path: credentials from the vault, then the body in the inbox.

33
00:01:51,261 --> 00:01:52,735
Both channels here are real.

34
00:01:52,735 --> 00:01:55,261
Every contact in the demo database is synthetic.

35
00:01:56,623 --> 00:02:00,804
The codebase is hexagonal Python: domain rules in the middle,

36
00:02:00,804 --> 00:02:03,203
FastAPI and providers at the edges.

37
00:02:04,021 --> 00:02:07,560
The prioritization policy interleaves companies.

38
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:10,656
The rate limiter enforces channel spacing.

39
00:02:10,656 --> 00:02:13,014
The vault encrypts SMTP secrets.

40
00:02:13,824 --> 00:02:17,334
Dispatch moves through prepared, sending, sent or failed,

41
00:02:17,334 --> 00:02:21,152
so a crash leaves a recovery record instead of a silent retry.

42
00:02:23,186 --> 00:02:28,306
FastAPI and SQLite, Camoufox for WhatsApp Web, SMTP for email.

43
00:02:28,306 --> 00:02:30,866
Everything runs on one machine.

44
00:02:31,587 --> 00:02:36,520
Real versus simulated: the application, dispatch pipeline and tests are real.

45
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:39,147
The companies and contacts are synthetic.

46
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:45,837
Reachout: two real channels, company-first pacing, and a record of every attempt.

47
00:02:46,287 --> 00:02:48,577
Two real sends, to the owner's own accounts.

48
00:02:48,577 --> 00:02:50,087
The repository link is below.
